meta {
  name: Get Data Health
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/market-data/:symbol/health?days_back=1
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  days_back: 1
  ~hours_back: 24
}

params:path {
  symbol: SPY
}

docs {
  Get data health check for a symbol (includes gap detection)

  Query params (provide EITHER hours_back OR days_back, not both):
  - days_back: Number of days to check (1-30)
  - hours_back: Number of hours to check (1-720)
  - Default: 24 hours (1 day) if neither specified

  Returns:
  - symbol: Trading symbol
  - hours_checked: Number of hours analyzed
  - bar_count: Total bars in time range
  - latest_bar_time: Timestamp of most recent bar (in configured timezone)
  - gap_count: Number of gaps detected
  - gaps: List of detected gaps with start/end times and missing bar counts
  - healthy: Boolean (false if gaps exist or no data)

  ⚠️ NOTE: The scheduled data_health_check job is DISABLED
  This endpoint must be called manually when needed because:
  - No database-backed issue tracking system exists yet
  - Scheduled job would log the same failures repeatedly (96+ duplicates/day)
  - No state tracking to detect when health status changes

  Use this for:
  - Manual data quality verification
  - Gap detection (replaces /gaps endpoint)
  - Checking data freshness (latest_bar_time)
  - Debugging data ingestion issues
  - One-time health analysis
}
